{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And this shall be the priests' due.</b> This section is joined to the one above, because there he mentioned that the Levites have no inheritance, and now he comes to say that the statutory gifts are their inheritance from YHWH, may He be exalted. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in tractate Ḥullin: ״מאת העם״ — 'from the people' — and not from the priests." "<b>From those who slaughter the slaughter.</b> The law applies to the slaughterer. <b>Whether ox or sheep,</b> to exclude the undomesticated animal (חיה). <b>The arm</b> (הזרוע), from the body, and it is from the joint of the elbow to the palm of the hand. <b>The cheeks</b> (הלחיים) — with the tongue — are from the head. <b>And the stomach</b> (והקיבה), from the entrails, among the internal organs. And these gifts are wholly ḥullin (unconsecrated), and therefore he did not mention them among all the priestly gifts in the section ויאמר ה' אל אהרן, for those that he mentioned there are consecrated, and therefore Scripture did not wish to mention the arm and the cheeks and the stomach — which are ḥullin — to mention them in the category of consecrated gifts. And even though it did not mention them explicitly, it alluded to them there, as it says (Numbers 18:12): ״ראשיתם אשר יתנו לה' לך נתתים״, and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״ראשית״ — this is the first of the fleece; ״אשר יתנו״ — these are the gifts of the arm and the cheeks and the stomach; ״לה'״ — this is the dough-offering (חלה). And the reason for these gifts: the arm corresponds to the hand, as it says (Numbers 25:7) ״ויקח רמח בידו״; the cheeks correspond to prayer, as it says (Psalms 106:30) ״ויעמוד פנחס ויפלל״; the stomach corresponds to (Numbers 25:8) ״האשה אל קבתה״; thus did our Rabbis of blessed memory interpret." "<b>And the Rambam</b>, of blessed memory, wrote concerning the reason for these gifts, that these limbs are ראשית (the first), and therefore they were given in honor of the blessed Name to His ministers: the cheeks are the first of the body, the arm is the first of the limbs that branch out from the body, the stomach is the first of the entrails."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:15.045434311Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}